<rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" version="2.0"><channel><title>visualization – justaddwater.dk</title><link>https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/tag/visualization/</link><description>Instant Usability &amp;amp; Web Standards — static archive</description><language>en-US</language><atom:link href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/tag/visualization/feed/" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" /><item><title>Interesting visualization of Money Flow</title><link>https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/2010/05/24/interesting-visualization-of-money-flow/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">http://justaddwater.dk/?p=1351</guid><dc:creator>Jesper Rønn-Jensen</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 24 May 2010 21:33:15 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;It is often said that an image is worth a thousand words. New York Times is a good resource for interesting visualization on current topics. The article on &lt;a href="http://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2010/05/02/weekinreview/02marsh.html"&gt;Europe’s Web of Debt&lt;/a&gt; is rather good at conveying a lot of information on the recent European Debt crisis. The width of the arrows and circles represents size of debt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2010/05/nytimes-european-debt-visualization-02marsh-image-custom1-v3.gif"&gt;&lt;img alt="" class="aligncenter size-medium wp-image-1350" height="296" sizes="(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" src="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2010/05/nytimes-european-debt-visualization-02marsh-image-custom1-v3-300x296.gif" srcset="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2010/05/nytimes-european-debt-visualization-02marsh-image-custom1-v3-300x296.gif 300w, https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2010/05/nytimes-european-debt-visualization-02marsh-image-custom1-v3.gif 970w" title="nytimes european debt visualization 02marsh-image-custom1-v3" width="300"/&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Earlier this year New York Times brought another interesting visualization: &lt;a href="http://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2010/01/10/nyregion/20100110-netflix-map.html"&gt;A Peek Into Netflix [rental] Queues&lt;/a&gt;, where you can explore where (by US postnumber) any top 100 movie gets rented. A standard US map is overlaid with a heatmap of the data, and combined with excerpts from the movie reviews. Very amusing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2010/01/10/nyregion/20100110-netflix-map.html"&gt;&lt;img alt="" class="aligncenter size-medium wp-image-1352" height="152" sizes="(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" src="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2010/05/Screen-shot-2010-05-24-at-11.25.16-PM-crop-300x152.png" srcset="https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2010/05/Screen-shot-2010-05-24-at-11.25.16-PM-crop-300x152.png 300w, https://watson.github.io/justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2010/05/Screen-shot-2010-05-24-at-11.25.16-PM-crop.png 931w" title="Screen shot 2010-05-24 at 11.25.16 PM crop" width="300"/&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
